From ef81efbfc7157caea6f67afa496899444cec3fc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:58:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): refuse manual release over unread foreign
 comments [daveey]

Manual promote/unblock previously consulted only lifecycle state, so a decision retracted after the caller read the thread could still be released. Enforce an optional seen-comment watermark, or the last 60 minutes by default, at CLI/tool boundaries under the status writer lock. List foreign comment provenance and a rerun command; exit 4 / unread_comments without mutations. Autonomous DB and owner-wake callers remain unchanged. Preserve bulk result reporting; a seen watermark is per-card, not shared across bulk ids.

Proof: requested baseline 29 tests passed; new suite RED on unchanged source (9 failed, 9 passed). GREEN: 222 tests across 11 files including all requested regressions and owner-wake, self-heal, missing-parent, CLI and tool consumers. No existing release fixture required a seen override. Session-context test verifies tool identity overrides process environment. Full scripts/check passed before main advanced; rerun after rebase required. Card t_9ef4956ed2ea24fe.
